1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,360
Brighten up the peace,
and try to step away from it.

2
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:27,020
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:31,500
Someone who heads straight
home once the night is over.

4
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:35,360
Wappara puwa, wappara.

5
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:39,960
Wappara boo wacchi wappara.

6
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:45,540
Don't rush, in this narrow little town.

7
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:49,380
Where are you off to? Haste makes waste,
so take the long way round.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:58,520
If, by any chance,
there's someone better than me,

9
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:03,000
tell me, tell me all through the night.

10
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:12,820
I don't mind waiting at all.

11
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:17,020
Because I'm a woman of Kame-za.

12
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,720
I won't lose, I'm a Ginza woman

13
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:26,520
I'll love you for years and years

14
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,880
It's the day of the Ginza woman

15
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,400
The secret of Charlie Kobayashi

16
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,140
Police chief for a day

17
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,200
I heard he's coming to the police box today

18
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,400
Who is it this time?

19
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,640
Is it Kyoko Fukada or Ryoko Hirose?

20
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,340
It's Charlie Kobayashi

21
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:53,220
Charlie Kobayashi?
What's that supposed to be?

22
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:54,160
A foreigner?

23
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:56,980
He's the vocalist of a visual-kei rock band

24
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:05,540
What?

25
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,760
Chief, what's that?

26
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,400
He's the police box chief for a day.

27
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,420
Bonjour!

28
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,620
Everyone at the Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,

29
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,580
What a flashy guy.

30
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,480
Everyone, please cooperate.

31
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:25,600
Charlie, please sign.

32
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,680
So they've already found us.

33
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,140
We can't compete with the fans

34
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:31,420
Showing up with a flashy band like that

35
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,340
If you all want autographs too,
go ahead and get them now.

36
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,720
I don't want an autograph or anything.

37
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:44,200
Honestly, I'd never seen or heard
of Charlie Kobayashi until just now,

38
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,320
Ryotsu, one-day chief, isn't that rude?

39
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:51,100
So are you saying the
Chief knew Charlie Kobayashi?

40
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,380
Well, that's...

41
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,680
See, the Chief doesn't
know him either, right?

42
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,880
So my popularity was fake after all.

43
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:00,315
The fans from earlier were all plants,

44
00:03:00,365 --> 00:03:04,280
and the office storeroom must be
full of returned CDs gathering dust!

45
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,370
You're overthinking it, Charlie.

46
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:09,940
Middle-aged folks are weak against visual-kei,
you know.

47
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,400
Hey, Pops,
you obviously know Charlie, right? Hey?

48
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:17,500
Yeah, on TV and in magazines a few times

49
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:18,400
You don't know him!

50
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,211
I remember now.
I'm in the entertainment world.

51
00:03:23,261 --> 00:03:26,460
Now that you mention it,
I've seen him all over the place.

52
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,260
R-really?

53
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:27,600
Yes.

54
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,340
No way, that's just flattery!

55
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,520
Charlie!

56
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,720
Thank you!

57
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,620
You bounce back fast, don't you?

58
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:53,840
Hey, you!

59
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:57,020
Charlie is a sensitive, delicate artist.

60
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,380
Please don't hurt him.

61
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:01,800
I'm sorry.

62
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,960
You see, I'm not very
well-versed in that sort of thing.

63
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,860
Don't make fun of me, Chief.

64
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:10,100
I do keep up with entertainment news too.

65
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,500
I just gave my honest opinion based on that.

66
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,640
Well, take a look at this.

67
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,640
Everything about visual-kei.

68
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,340
Ready?

69
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:22,700
Among the visual-kei bands that
dominate Japan's current music scene,

70
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:25,060
our Charlie Kobayashi with Narcissist

71
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,800
our Charlie Kobayashi with Narcissist

72
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,520
This isn't it either.

73
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,100
Not this one either.

74
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:36,040
That's strange...

75
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,260
It's not listed anywhere!

76
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,000
Found it!

77
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,000
Where?

78
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:40,980
Right here, right here.

79
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:43,268
I see,

80
00:04:43,318 --> 00:04:46,900
so he's a last-minute visual-kei
act jumping on the bandwagon.

81
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,400
Call him the headliner. The headliner!

82
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,720
In short, he's just a copycat.

83
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:57,740
Squeezing this in between your busy schedule,
including recording your new single,

84
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:00,640
you've agreed to be our one-day police chief,
haven't you?

85
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:03,600
Yes, it's a chance to
get up close with the fans.

86
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,020
Well then, I'm taking the picture now.

87
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:08,720
Forensics

88
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:16,360
Not that my gravure shoot is anything special.
The best I can hope for is the forensics photographer taking my picture.

89
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:21,400
Gravure? This is a black-and-white photo for
the Katsushika Police Station's PR newsletter.

90
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:40,960
Alright, since I'm the chief anyway,
let's pick a cool costume.

91
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,580
How about something like this?

92
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,720
It's completely different from
the Katsushika box's uniform.

93
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,720
Visual-kei must be tough.

94
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:55,960
It's the burden of a man born beautiful.

95
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,740
I don't expect you to understand, though.

96
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:01,820
Why, you're just a bandwagon visual-kei act.

97
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:04,500
So that's really how the world sees him.

98
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,060
Someone like me... someone like me...

99
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:07,120
Chari

100
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,360
Enough with the unnecessary stuff!

101
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:11,880
What's wrong with that?

102
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:13,460
Budget, Ryotsu!

103
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,720
C-Chari?

104
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:31,960
Thank you!

105
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,920
Well, let's take the pictures.

106
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:41,700
Wait!

107
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,520
What's wrong, Charlie?

108
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:46,200
I'm a bit tired,
let's take a break around here.

109
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:46,940
Got it.

110
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,920
Yeah, yeah, yeah, got it.

111
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:56,900
I'm sorry, but could you refrain
from taking photos of this person?

112
00:06:56,900 --> 00:07:00,640
Why? Nakagawa is also an
officer at this police box.

113
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:01,960
Well, actually...

114
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:04,240
I don't mind, though.

115
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:04,960
Thanks.

116
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:08,920
Basically, you don't want to stand
next to the handsome Nakagawa, right?

117
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:13,160
Charlie, you don't have the confidence
to beat Nakagawa in a two-shot, do you?

118
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,080
Senpai

119
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:19,620
A civil servant like you, what's gotten into you?
He's so cool...

120
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:22,380
Charlie, don't pay attention to
every little thing that guy says.

121
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:26,220
Ryotsu, stop butting in every single time.

122
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:28,700
It'll only make things more complicated!

123
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:32,500
Nakagawa's not allowed, but it's
fine if it's me, Terai, or Chief Ohara

124
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:35,600
Don't you think that's pretty rude, Chief?

125
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:36,780
W-well, that's...

126
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:56,620
Alright, good. Charlie, you're beautiful.

127
00:07:56,620 --> 00:08:04,500
You're cool, I'm beautiful, I'm cool. Yes, you're beautiful.
You won't lose, and I won't lose to anyone!

128
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,820
I won't lose!

129
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:14,960
Visual-kei that loses to a regular civilian isn't visual-kei at all,
Charlie!

130
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:37,920
Listen, Charlie, you're the only
down-to-earth visual-kei act in the country.

131
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:41,640
You're the only relatable
visual-kei act out there.

132
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:46,520
Because you're the only visual-kei
act who's been a one-day police chief.

133
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,200
Only me?

134
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,960
That's right, only you.
Have some confidence!

135
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,960
I don't get it.

136
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:59,400
Yeah, that's the plan. After the visual-kei band festival is over,
let's go record in Nashville like we talked about ages ago.

137
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:04,840
Really? Then let's resume the shoot right away.
Okay, Nakagawa, please.

138
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:06,100
Yes.

139
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,940
In the end, you didn't even let
us get Nakagawa's face in the shot!

140
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:18,200
Thanks to you, I had a great time.

141
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,620
Likewise,
sorry we had nothing much to offer you.

142
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:24,720
All that fuss just to take
photos and be one-day chief?

143
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:27,480
Even the idol went along on patrol.

144
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:30,260
At this rate, you're not a one-day chief,
you're a three-minute chief.

145
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:32,080
No, you're a photo chief.

146
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,460
Well then, Ryotsu.

147
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,360
Charlie.

148
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,100
We've got the rock festival
rehearsal coming up.

149
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,100
Mr. Charlie.

150
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,500
You misunderstand visual-kei.

151
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,440
No, I'm not talking about visual-kei, I'm...

152
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:45,080
I'm mocking you personally, you shady guy.

153
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,280
W-where am I shady?

154
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,260
All of it. You reek of it.

155
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:49,640
What?

156
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,160
Don't bother with Charlie.

157
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:56,440
I have to do this for my many fans
and the other visual-kei bands too,

158
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,700
I can't go home with
people misunderstanding me.

159
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,840
So the other bands have
nothing to do with it.

160
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,120
Knock it off, Ryotsu!

161
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:02,720
Ryo-san.

162
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:06,120
Fine, I'll join your tour for half a day.

163
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,580
It's a patrol.

164
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:13,720
It's been a while since I walked the common folk's streets.
Not bad.

165
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:14,800
Yes!

166
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:20,680
They say I'm a popular artist, but no one's
come up to me one by one since earlier Cherry?

167
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:23,840
They say there's a warm atmosphere.

168
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,740
But from now on,
I'm a down-to-earth music type,

169
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,060
A down-to-earth music type

170
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:39,100
That's an honest opinion.

171
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:40,240
Anyway, I'm

172
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,020
a chef.

173
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:58,400
It's nothing.

174
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,840
They're just elementary schoolers
in their mischievous phase.

175
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,120
Don't mind it, don't mind it.

176
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,460
Atta boy, Charlie!

177
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:07,740
Let's head to the bookstore next and check
how Charlie's autobiography is selling.

178
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:08,300
Okay.

179
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:11,120
Geez, being a manager must be tough.

180
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:14,940
Found it?

181
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,700
Nope, it's nowhere.

182
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:20,020
They probably didn't stock a
single copy of my book anyway.

183
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,680
Here we go again, hey, manager!

184
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,920
Right! It must have sold out completely!

185
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,760
Charlie, yes, that's great!
That's exactly it!

186
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:43,700
You two really are a great team as always!

187
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,700
There it is!

188
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,300
Let's see, let's see. Charlie's profile?

189
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:54,420
Born in London in 1978

190
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,840
It's already here!

191
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:59,900
Born to an Italian-French father
and a second-generation Japanese mother,

192
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:02,960
he spent his childhood in Switzerland,
the Netherlands, and Russia.

193
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,600
After his father's death,
he moved to Japan, his mother's homeland,

194
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,540
After being baptized,
he's arrived at the present day,

195
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:11,400
forcing himself to put on a mysterious air,

196
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:13,980
it seems he's trying to
throw the masses off the scent.

197
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:15,140
Ugh, come on.

198
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,360
Please stop with the weird suspicions.

199
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,760
Well then,
let's get the signature right away.

200
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:19,200
Excuse me...

201
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,620
Sir/Ma'am,

202
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,100
that's a book being returned.

203
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:24,140
Could you please not
touch it without permission?

204
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,520
Returned?

205
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:28,440
It's broken now.

206
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:48,240
Hmph, great artists are always
treated with respect by their era.

207
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:51,340
I've been thinking about
this for a while now.

208
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:54,460
I've seen your face somewhere before,
long ago.

209
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:58,340
W-well, that's because you're
everywhere in the media, Charlie.

210
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:01,720
No, further back,
when I was still a student.

211
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,220
W-w-wh-what is this guy talking about?

212
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:03,920
Ahahaha.

213
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,880
Wait, I think I'm about
to remember something.

214
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,680
That's it, let's go check over there.

215
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,620
Where is it, where is it?

216
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,620
A, i, u, e, o.

217
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,540
Ka, ki, ku, ke, ko.

218
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:21,544
Sa, shi, su, se, so.

219
00:13:21,594 --> 00:13:24,060
Ta, chi, chi, cha, chari.

220
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,980
Found it, found my C.T.!

221
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:26,820
Of course.

222
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:27,900
Found one over here too!

223
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,840
Used records corner?

224
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:36,650
Twenty years ago, he vanished
after releasing just one hit song,

225
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:39,020
a poor folk singer.

226
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:42,640
His name was, his name was,
his name was Kazuo Kobayashi.

227
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:48,580
Charlie Kobayashi,
your true identity from twenty years ago!

228
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,600
No, you've got the wrong person.

229
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,360
I have rehearsal now,
so I'll be taking my leave.

230
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,520
Come on, let's go.

231
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:58,680
Wait!

232
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:03,240
There's no mistake, it's Kazuo Kobayashi.

233
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,280
I know this record.

234
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,260
I remember buying it back in the day.

235
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:11,300
It was one of the hits from the folk boom era,
after all.

236
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:15,920
It's from Kazuo Kobayashi, the one-hit wonder
who burst onto the scene and faded just as fast.

237
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:19,780
If these two are the same person,
isn't he around the same age as Ryo-chan?

238
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:23,860
Well, lying about your age
isn't rare in show business.

239
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,880
He fabricated his entire profile,

240
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,770
then jumped on the visual-kei band boom.

241
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:32,151
He hid his face with makeup
and made a comeback as a rookie.

242
00:14:32,201 --> 00:14:34,260
I'm impressed by his sheer nerve.

243
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,000
But when you think about it,
that's an incredible obsession.

244
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:38,940
The effort he put in is
no small thing, either.

245
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:42,539
Still, that Charlie having
this other face all along,

246
00:14:42,589 --> 00:14:44,300
if it got out to the public,
it would be a huge deal, wouldn't it?

247
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,444
No, there's no need to worry about that.

248
00:14:46,494 --> 00:14:49,620
I tried to sell the story to the media,
but they turned me down.

249
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,920
Charlie Kobayashi's story?

250
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:54,200
No thanks, no thanks.

251
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,540
Apparently he's not very popular either.

252
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:58,880
Scum.

253
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,360
That's cruel, Ryo-san.

254
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:04,320
We were partners enough that he was briefly police chief for a day,
weren't we?

255
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,320
Senpai.

256
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,560
That's why I said it didn't sell.

257
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:10,980
Still, come to think of it,
that guy's a pitiful man.

258
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:12,200
What?

259
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:16,660
Hey, what happened?

260
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,380
Isn't that Charlie?

261
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:21,460
This is bad.

262
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:22,520
Are you all right?

263
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,920
No way.

264
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,640
Don't say such unlucky things.

265
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:30,040
Looks like you weren't hurt

266
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:33,300
But how did an accident happen on
a road with such good visibility?

267
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:35,600
The moment I saw that smoke,
all of a sudden -

268
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,560
This road is still in better shape.

269
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:43,980
You must have been really
scared of meeting Ryo-san.

270
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:47,960
Your annoying manager isn't with you today?

271
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:51,640
My manager went ahead to the venue.

272
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,780
Y-yeah, we don't have time for this.

273
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:55,780
I have to go.

274
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,460
The car!

275
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,400
Where are you going?

276
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:01,680
We're headed to the band festival now.

277
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,560
Band festival?

278
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:07,760
No answer.

279
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:08,680
What's he doing?

280
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:09,400
Hello?

281
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,480
Charlie, pick up already!

282
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:11,220
Hello?

283
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,540
H-hey, what are you doing?

284
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:19,720
To think he couldn't make
his concert because of me...

285
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,980
I'd hate for him to start
making some weird accusations.

286
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,600
I'll make sure he gets
into the venue properly.

287
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,140
You don't need to see me off.

288
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,180
I've just arranged an equipment van.

289
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:31,100
The rest of you,
please ride over there with the brats.

290
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:32,100
Understood.

291
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,940
I'll go along with everyone too.

292
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,020
Calm down.

293
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:36,660
Bring the van out.

294
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:37,540
Right.

295
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:41,900
I haven't told anyone about that
except the guys at the police box.

296
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,220
What are you talking about?

297
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,860
We're on Charlie's side.

298
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,880
Quite a crowd

299
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:52,980
Of course, all of Japan's
visual-kei bands are gathered here.

300
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,720
I'm putting everything
into today's live show.

301
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,640
Go for a comeback hit.

302
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,120
I'm Charlie.

303
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:03,020
Nakagawa,
pull up to the dressing room entrance.

304
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:04,440
It's probably the back entrance.

305
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,000
Understood.

306
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:09,200
Admission has already started.

307
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,320
I think it's around here.

308
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,760
Isn't that it?

309
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:17,080
Well, we're heading back now.

310
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:18,680
We wish you success.

311
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:19,200
Thanks.

312
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,060
I misjudged you.

313
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,160
Don't worry about it.

314
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,860
Nakagawa, bring the van around.

315
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:27,000
See you, Kazuo Kobayashi.

316
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:31,860
I told you! Aaaaaah!

317
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:36,820
Staff members, hey! Turn right at the end of this hall,
it's on the left. Thanks.

318
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:41,620
Alright. So all sorts of superstars
have walked down this hallway?

319
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:45,120
This is getting absurd, I must say.

320
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,140
me

321
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,180
Charlie still hasn't reached the hall?

322
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:58,440
Yeah, I just heard from his manager -

323
00:17:58,440 --> 00:17:59,320
Let me try calling.

324
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:03,360
This is Ryotsu. We definitely delivered
him right to the backstage entrance.

325
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,860
He hasn't come, has he?
He really hasn't come.

326
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:09,100
If Charlie doesn't show up, Wanda's
going to take responsibility for this.

327
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:11,780
Where the hell did that guy go?

328
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,560
I've calmed down a little.

329
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:18,220
Okay.

330
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:21,800
The band two before them
has already finished, too.

331
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:23,460
Where on earth did he go?

332
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,800
Charlie Kobayashi with Narcissist, everyone!

333
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,980
Please stand by.

334
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:29,900
Yes, Charlie.

335
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,400
Good morning.

336
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,700
Well, look at that, it's Kobayashi!

337
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,520
What are you doing these days, Kobayashi?

338
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:38,580
No, I'm Charlie!

339
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:41,500
I came all fired up, but...

340
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:43,300
You're not wearing that costume today

341
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:43,740
Yeah, yeah.

342
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:45,360
Come on, let's change over here.

343
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:49,800
Think they'll let us in?

344
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:51,420
You lot!

345
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:54,500
Where the hell did you take him?

346
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:57,500
We definitely dropped him
off at the back entrance here.

347
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:58,380
Back entrance?

348
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,120
Senpai, I'll go take a look.

349
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:01,540
Hey.

350
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:03,980
What, he still hasn't arrived?

351
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,620
He'll be here any moment,
so please wait a little longer.

352
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:09,060
We've already moved your
performance slot back two spots,

353
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:11,480
but we can't change the order any further.

354
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:11,980
Yeah.

355
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:15,200
We only agreed to book you

356
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:18,220
because your agency's president personally begged us.
What's the big idea?

357
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:20,660
I'm sorry, I'm really sorry.

358
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:21,920
We'll wait five more minutes.

359
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:24,460
If he's not here in five minutes,
he's cancelled.

360
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:24,880
Right.

361
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,080
Sorry to keep you waiting.

362
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,080
Th-th-the...

363
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,900
I'm Charlie Kobayashi.

364
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:31,960
Ryo.

365
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,740
Y-you're Charlie?

366
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,480
Have you put on some weight?

367
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:37,180
Ha-ha-ha!

368
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,460
No, I quit smoking,
so I seem to have gained a little weight.

369
00:19:41,030 --> 00:19:42,220
What on earth is this act supposed to be?

370
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,700
I am Charlie.

371
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,560
And now,
we'll have Kazuo Kobayashi sing for us.

372
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,080
"Tokyo Hustle Man."

373
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:50,080
Hustle away, please!

374
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:59,840
What did you say?

375
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:03,700
The Tokyo I longed for,

376
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:08,560
the Tokyo I dreamed of,

377
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:13,360
you came to Tokyo, didn't you?

378
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:19,380
We've got to hustle, hustle,
hustle, or it means nothing.

379
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:24,160
Just the two of us at Tokyo Tower,

380
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:28,940
just the two of us on a Hato Bus tour.

381
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:35,220
Even though it's the hustle
rendezvous I dreamed of,

382
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:38,620
now you're someone else's wife.

383
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:46,760
Bittersweet Tokyo, Tokyo, hustle man.

384
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:55,780
This is a disaster.

385
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,180
What?

386
00:20:58,740 --> 00:21:00,260
Take off!

387
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:01,780
Alright, that's it!

388
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:02,920
Da-da-daa!

389
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,000
Whoa!

390
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:08,520
Just sing something!

391
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,940
Ugh! This is getting so annoying!

392
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,320
Hey-hey heart!

393
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:17,120
Hey! Arrest him, arrest him!

394
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,100
Grab him!

395
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:21,740
Ugh! I'm serving a life sentence for love!

396
00:21:21,740 --> 00:21:22,760
Yeah!

397
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,320
I saw a window in my dream.

398
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:28,080
Hazu love action nano.

399
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:29,700
I...

400
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:31,680
someone else's wife.

401
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:35,560
The aching Tokyo.

402
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:39,940
Tokyo, hustling man.

403
00:21:54,300 --> 00:22:01,360
So the back door we thought was Kameari Hall was
actually the dressing room entrance of Kameari Public Hall

404
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:06,920
I love you, I love you,
I love you in the Sightseeing Corps.

405
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:09,420
I love him so much I'd even stake him out.

406
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:12,320
Wow, amazing!

407
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:18,300
As always, there are so many flashy bands.

408
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:20,780
Speaking of which,
I wonder what happened to Charlie?

409
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:24,440
Even after switching to visual kei,
he was still a one-hit wonder.

410
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:28,700
I guess not being able to play
the band festival was a big blow.

411
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:31,380
It'd be sad if he just
disappeared like this.

412
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:33,200
That's his fate.

413
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:36,540
Doesn't matter, but would you take
that makeup off already, Ryo-chan?

414
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:40,640
Nonsense! I'm the one who had every
customer in the main hall fighting over me.

415
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,720
Do you think this makeup comes off easily?

416
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,560
And thanks to this,
I don't have to take a bath.

417
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:46,480
Gross.

418
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:48,320
Trouble!

419
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,240
What happened?

420
00:22:50,060 --> 00:22:52,360
Now, I'll introduce today's
one-day station chief.

421
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:55,260
It's folk singer Kazuo Kobayashi.

422
00:22:55,260 --> 00:22:56,660
Kazuo Kobayashi.

423
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:02,160
The Tokyo I've longed for,

424
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:07,080
the Tokyo I dreamed of,

425
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:17,980
now that I've come to Tokyo, I've got to hustle,
hustle, hustle, or there's no point!

426
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:27,400
Just you and me in Tokyo,
just you and me on a sightseeing bus tour,

427
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:33,820
the hustling rendezvous I dreamed about, yet

428
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:37,180
you're already someone else's wife.

429
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,860
The painful Tokyo,

430
00:23:42,260 --> 00:23:43,200
Tokyo.

431
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:46,600
At the end of a long
journey searching for myself,

432
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:51,480
Kazuo Kobayashi reached
a longed-for place of rest.

433
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:55,440
How wonderful is life.

434
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:36,040
After every fight, we share a brief kiss.

435
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:40,180
You, with your teary eyes,
were so dear to me.

436
00:24:40,180 --> 00:24:45,440
Such irreplaceable things,

437
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:50,860
how many of them does a
person ever get in a lifetime?

438
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:57,160
You are me, and I am you.

439
00:24:58,140 --> 00:25:02,240
That alone was enough to fulfill me.

440
00:25:03,320 --> 00:25:08,300
Just from you smiling, look,

441
00:25:08,790 --> 00:25:14,900
it felt like every pain was healed.

442
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:22,980
It's you again, Professor Tondemo!

443
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:25,300
This time it's a deep-sea suit experiment!

444
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,100
I said no, damn it!

445
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,520
Wait a minute...

446
00:25:29,520 --> 00:25:30,920
If it's this, then maybe...

447
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:33,740
we could take all the treasure
from sunken ships we want!

448
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:36,460
Next time: Tondemo Deep Sea SOS!

449
00:25:36,460 --> 00:25:37,340
See you then!

